> 
>In the Artifacts list, weapons appear like this -
> 
>Name		Weapon Type		  Special       	What	Al
>--------------------------------------------------------------------------
>Dragonbane	|Broadsword	| 5 | x2 |		       |dragon | N
>Excalibur	|Long sword	| 5 | 10 | seek,def,search     |       | L
>
> [What does it all mean?]

Here is the definitive answer:
Dragonbane does +(some random number between 1 and 5) to hit above normal
enchantment and 2 times damage including enchantment against dragons only!
(See the "what" column.)  If you have a +5 Dragonbane, you're well-off
against dragons. {+[6-10] to hit, and (longsword vs. large + 5) x 2 damage.}



BUT, and not many people know this:
Excalibur does +(some random number between 1 and 5) to hit above enchantment,
and +(some random number between 1 and 10) to hit against everything.  
NOT +10.  So you're better off with artifacts that do x2 damage if they're
highly enchanted.

That's the general rule for artifacts.  x2 damage means roll up damage once,
add normal enchantment, and multiply the result by two.  
+[constant damage] means roll up damage once, and normal enchantment, and
add a random number bewteen 1 and [constant damage] inclusive.

